# Prototype Kit Reuse

When designing or implementing an AI-generated prototype:

1. Before writing UI, automatically select the smallest applicable design workflow:
   - Kit covers the page → `toptop-design-system`
   - Kit has page-level gaps → `toptop-prototype-studio`
   - Screenshot-to-component mapping → `page-canvas-vision`
   - Extra craft/a11y review → use `ui-skills-root` to select at most one relevant specialist Skill
   External Skills may refine uncovered areas but must never override TopTop Foundations or stable Kit contracts.
2. Run a visual-foundation preflight. Read only the relevant entries from:
   - `specs/foundations/colors.yaml`
   - `specs/foundations/spacing.yaml`
   - `specs/foundations/typography.yaml`
   - `specs/foundations/icons.yaml`
   - `specs/foundations/radius.yaml` and `motion.yaml` when applicable
   - matching component YAML, MDX, interaction YAML, and `components/kit` implementation
   Write down the intended component, Token, spacing, and size mapping before styling.
   For every reused component, follow its `interactionIds` into `specs/interactions/<id>.yaml` and `content/interactions/<id>.mdx`. The Portal `/interactions` section is the human-readable index; YAML remains the contract source.
3. Reuse existing Kit components whenever the design contains their responsibility:
   - Tags and badges → `list-tag`
   - Action or message rows → `regular-list`
   - Page title bars and tabs → the matching navigation component
   - Search → `SearchControl`; do not add a wrapper that changes its 56pt container, 40pt field, 16pt gutter, or Token background
   - Icons → `SystemIcon`, `BottomNavigationIcon`, `SearchControl`, or extend `generate-inline-icon-assets.mjs`; never CSS mask or rasterized SVG `<img>` (see `prototype-asset-pipeline.mdc`)
   - Avatars & prototype photos → `PrototypeAvatarImage` / `AvatarVisual` with @3x bitmaps registered in `generate-prototype-avatar-3x.mjs`
4. Do not recreate or restyle Kit internals. Prototype CSS may position the component but must not add duplicate padding, height, gap, color, typography, radius, or icon rules to descendants such as `.regularListMain` or `.searchControlField`.
5. Use semantic Tokens for every reusable visual value. Examples: page/list background → `color.surface.canvas` (`bgPrimary`); panel → `color.surface.panel`; text/icon color → the matching `color.text.*`. Brand primary defaults to `color.brand.primary` (`#16D8C8`) for every new page and unspecified region/package; `color.ku.*` and `color.brand.tw-*` require explicit product context. Raw values are allowed only inside an isolated `Prototype*` gap with a documented reason.
6. If no Kit component can express a required area, design it as a clearly named `Prototype*` module using Foundations Tokens, record the `kitGap`, and do not invent a componentId or mark it stable.
7. Reuse interaction patterns as strictly as visual components. Preserve documented states, trigger → result transitions, feedback, duration/easing, dismiss behavior, focus restoration, keyboard behavior, error recovery, localization, and edge cases. Do not add a prototype-local gesture or overlay when an existing Pattern already covers it. Missing behavior becomes an explicit interaction `kitGap`.
8. Before handoff, verify actual rendered DOM values and behavior at the target viewport—not only source code:
   - component bounds, page gutter, padding, gap, fixed insets, and safe area
   - computed colors resolve to the intended semantic Tokens
   - icons resolve through the canonical registry and Kit wrapper
   - every applicable Pattern state and transition, including pressed/focus, loading/error/empty, dismiss, focus return, and reduced motion
   Any local CSS override that makes a Kit component fail its YAML dimensions must be removed.
9. Include component/Token/interactionId mapping, DOM and behavior evidence, unresolved `kitGaps`, and tests run in the handoff.
